        "id": 1054778
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T17:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Change Ib522a86 introduced an explicit test to ensure wrong case doesn\u0027t match.\nI guess it might be a legacy use case, however I am wanted to make sure to be back compatible.\n\n@ekempin@google.com do you recall what was the use case for that test?",
      "parentUuid": "ae4a0f6e_d08c7480",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44563834_917ac07b",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T22:13:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@nasser.grainawi@oss.qualcomm.com I believe this behaviour came from the transition of the accounts table into the `All-Users.git` repository, with the concept of having the e-mail as secondary id.\n\nIf you have User@Company.com and user@company.com in the external-ids, they will result in different notedb ids.\n\nHowever, Lucene returns case-insensitive matching, therefore @ekempin@google.com introduced a further check for exact matching as post-processing from Lucene.\n\nBottom line: we can\u0027t just _fix the bug_ as-is IMHO, as we\u0027ve been relying on this bug since Gerrit v2.14 (over 12 releases ago).",
      "parentUuid": "d24c9d04_a2a2ce99",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84ba64d1_30942f94",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T22:13:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is counter-intuitive: I would expect a feature to be enabled when you set a flag to true, but here we enable the case-insensitive matching when the flag is set to false.\n\nWe should be consistent with the approach we took for the case-insensitive username matching, see https://gerrit-documentation.storage.googleapis.com/Documentation/3.10.2/config-gerrit.html#auth.userNameCaseInsensitive",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
